{
 "name": "R1-08-core-invitee-revives-a-grant-she-stopped-updates",
 "note": "bea is invited as host and stops the invitation herself (updates of the invitation: her own stop, no power needed), then answers accepted with the stop in her past. circles.md: \"A stopped grant stays stopped; rejoining needs a new grant.\" Oracle: bea is not a member (and is listed in `removed` with null, which circles.md says an invitation stopped before it is answered should not be). Core: bea is a member with the invitation's roles and a note she signs as the circle speaks for it (fold.rs: an own stop before any head is dropped because `who` is read from live heads, fold.rs:1182, and the `answers` stop needs a head, fold.rs:1143).",
 "steps": 7,
